    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nI propose adding support for brace expansion within the `mini.files` buffer to streamline the creation of multiple files and folders. This feature would significantly enhance workflow efficiency to create multiple files or directories in one go.\r\n\r\n**Examples:**\r\n\r\n1. **Directory Creation**\r\n    **Input:** `test/{foo,bar}`\r\n    **Result:** Creates directories `test/foo` and `test/bar`\r\n\r\n2. **File Creation with Extensions**\r\n    **Input:** `test/{foo.lua, bar.lua}`\r\n    **Result:** Creates files `test/foo.lua` and `test/bar.lua`\r\n\r\n3. **Nested Directories and Files**\r\n    **Input:** `test/{foo,bar}/foo.lua`\r\n    **Result:** Creates directories `test/foo` and `test/bar`, and files `test/foo/foo.lua` and `test/bar/foo.lua`",
